load(":cases.bzl", "adopt_deps_case")

# `mojo_adopted_library` holds its `deps` to the closure of its `lib` (the packages `[dependencies]` of the
# package's mopm.toml brings, here komira_resources' one sibling, komira_runtime_paths), one case per
# `-c adopt_deps.case=<case>`:
#   missing  deps = []                              Must FAIL: `lib` is built from komira_runtime_paths, `deps` does not bring it
#   extra    deps = [runtime_paths, komira_json]    Must FAIL: `deps` brings komira_json, `lib` is not built from it
#   agree    deps = [runtime_paths]                 Must BUILD: the control, so the two refusals are about the lists
#   native_unshipped         adopted library with `c_deps`, no `native_static`; a dependent's closure check states no unshipped C
#                                                 Must FAIL: the closure links the C and no library of it ships it
#   native_unshipped_stated  the same, the check stating the C as unshipped
#                                                 Must BUILD: the control, so the refusal above is about the state of the closure
#   native_static            the same library with `native_static = True`, the check stating none
#                                                 Must BUILD: the library ships the C as a static archive, the dependent's closure finds its owner
# With no case set the package declares only its doc_tree, so loading it never fails by accident. The
# scenario is tools/build/selftest:analysis_refusals_adopt_deps.
adopt_deps_case()
